# Hand edits to the parsed chronicle, applied by parse_entries.py after every
# rule has run. Append-only: never rewrite a line, add a new one.
#
# Keyed by (leaf, anchor), where the anchor is the opening of the entry with
# case and accents removed -- NOT the entry's index, which renumbers whenever
# any rule above it changes. If the consensus improves and the text under an
# anchor moves, the edit stops matching and parse_entries reports it as
# ORPHANED rather than quietly dropping it: a decision that no longer knows
# what it was deciding has to be made again.
#
# What belongs here: decisions a parser cannot reach. What does not: anything
# that generalises (that is a rule, where it can be measured), and anything
# that changes what a word *says* (that is the adjudication, with the facsimile
# on screen -- see docs/EDITORIAL.md).
#
# ops: "drop" removes the entry; "date" sets its month and day.
